# TSL `.toVar()`

In `three/tsl` graphs, **nodes are expressions**. Reusing a node without `.toVar()` can emit the same subgraph multiple times. Assign intermediates with `.toVar('name')`.

```ts
// prefer — compute once, reuse, readable WGSL/GLSL names
const wipeField = texMask.sample(screenUv).r.toVar("wipeField");
const mixFactor = softProgress
  .smoothstep(wipeField.sub(uEdge), wipeField.add(uEdge))
  .toVar("mixFactor");

// avoid — opaque names, wipeField / sample may be duplicated in the graph
const f = texMask.sample(uv()).r;
const t = p.smoothstep(f.sub(uEdge), f.add(uEdge));
```

## When to use

- Intermediate used **more than once** (`.sub` + `.add`, mix args, etc.)
- Value **mutated** later (`.assign` / `.addAssign` inside `Loop` / `Fn`) — required
- Non-trivial step worth a **stable debug name** in generated shaders

## When to skip

- Single-use throwaway in a short chain: `positionLocal.mul(uScale)` passed once into a call

Always pass a string name: `.toVar('heightNormalized')`, not bare `.toVar()`.
